                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe vulnerability identified as **CVE-2021-29533** affects the `tensorflow-gpu` package, specifically version `2.1.0`, which is a part of the TensorFlow library. This vulnerability arises from an issue in the implementation of certain operations that can lead to a denial of service (DoS) or potentially allow for arbitrary code execution. The root cause is improper validation of input data, which can lead to buffer overflows or other memory corruption issues.\n\n### Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: Update to a version of TensorFlow that has addressed this vulnerability. The TensorFlow team has released patches in later versions, so upgrading to the latest stable release is advised.\n\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement strict input validation to ensure that all inputs are within expected ranges and formats. This can help prevent malformed data from triggering the vulnerability.\n\n3. **Use Security Tools**: Employ static analysis and other security tools to detect potential vulnerabilities in your codebase.\n\n4. **Monitor Dependencies**: Regularly check for updates and security advisories related to your project's dependencies.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe TensorFlow team has addressed this issue in later versions by adding proper input validation and bounds checking. If you are unable to upgrade, consider backporting these changes to your version. Here is a general approach to fixing such issues:\n\n```python\n# Example of input validation\ndef safe_operation(input_data):\n    if not isinstance(input_data, expected_type):\n        raise ValueError(\"Invalid input type\")\n    if not (min_value <= input_data <= max_value):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input out of bounds\")\n    # Proceed with operation\n```\n\n### Relevant Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration\n\nThis vulnerability is related to the following CWE:\n\n- [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)\n\nPlease ensure that you are following best practices for secure coding and regularly updating your dependencies to mitigate such vulnerabilities."
