              "id": "glog-72c30980-eea6-4467-adf2-a674577459f3",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\n**CVE-2015-4840** is a vulnerability in the Java SE component of Oracle Java SE (subcomponent: Libraries). It is applicable to versions 7u85 and earlier, and 8u60 and earlier. This vulnerability allows remote attackers to affect confidentiality, integrity, and availability via unknown vectors related to the Libraries component. The issue is due to improper handling of serialized data, which can lead to deserialization of untrusted data, potentially allowing attackers to execute arbitrary code.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Update Java**: Ensure that you are using the latest version of Java, as Oracle has released patches to address this vulnerability.\n2. **Limit Deserialization**: Avoid deserializing data from untrusted sources. If deserialization is necessary, use a library that provides additional security checks.\n3. **Use a Security Manager**: Implement a Java Security Manager to restrict the actions that can be performed by untrusted code.\n4. **Input Validation**: Validate and sanitize all inputs before processing them, especially if they are used in deserialization.\n5. **Network Segmentation**: Isolate systems that process serialized data from untrusted sources to limit potential damage.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo mitigate the risk of deserialization vulnerabilities, consider using a library like `Gson` or `Jackson` for JSON processing, which does not rely on Java serialization. If you must use Java serialization, consider implementing a custom `ObjectInputStream` to filter classes that can be deserialized.\n\n```java\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.io.InputStream;\nimport java.io.ObjectInputStream;\nimport java.io.ObjectStreamClass;\n\npublic class SafeObjectInputStream extends ObjectInputStream {\n\n    public SafeObjectInputStream(InputStream in) throws IOException {\n        super(in);\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    protected Class<?> resolveClass(ObjectStreamClass desc) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {\n        String className = desc.getName();\n        if (!isAllowedClass(className)) {\n            throw new ClassNotFoundException(\"Unauthorized deserialization attempt: \" + className);\n        }\n        return super.resolveClass(desc);\n    }\n\n    private boolean isAllowedClass(String className) {\n        // Implement your logic to allow only specific classes\n        return className.startsWith(\"com.yourcompany.\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Deserialization Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Deserialization_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Top Ten 2021](https://owasp.org/Top10/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2015-4840/suse:java:"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
