              "id": "glog-b8629e22-702c-4b96-b31d-20060d40a581",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\n\r\nCVE-2015-4760 is a vulnerability found in the Java SE component of Oracle Java SE (subcomponent: Libraries). It allows remote attackers to affect confidentiality, integrity, and availability via unknown vectors related to the Libraries component. This vulnerability is particularly concerning as it can be exploited over a network without requiring user credentials, making it a critical issue for systems relying on Java SE.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n\r\n1. **Update Java SE**: Ensure that you are using the latest version of Java SE, as Oracle regularly releases patches that address known vulnerabilities.\r\n2. **Network Segmentation**: Limit exposure by segmenting your network to restrict access to critical systems that use Java SE.\r\n3. **Input Validation**: Implement strict input validation to prevent malicious data from being processed by your Java applications.\r\n4. **Security Monitoring**: Use intrusion detection systems to monitor for unusual activity that may indicate an exploitation attempt.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\n\r\nWhile the specific details of the vulnerability are not disclosed, general best practices for securing Java applications include:\r\n\r\n- **Use Secure Libraries**: Ensure that all third-party libraries are up-to-date and do not contain known vulnerabilities.\r\n- **Exception Handling**: Implement comprehensive exception handling to prevent the application from crashing or leaking sensitive information.\r\n- **Code Review**: Conduct regular code reviews to identify and fix potential security issues.\r\n\r\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\r\n\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n\r\n- [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)\r\n\r\nPlease ensure that you regularly check for updates and patches from Oracle and apply them promptly to mitigate potential risks associated with this vulnerability."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2015-4760/suse:java:"
                ]
              }
            },
