              "id": "glog-70120ede-3ff2-489d-8854-4595aa9ece76",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\n\r\n**Vulnerability CVE-2021-35588** affects the Java package and is related to improper input validation. This vulnerability allows an attacker to exploit the application by providing specially crafted input that the application does not properly validate. This can lead to unexpected behavior, including potential data corruption or unauthorized access to sensitive information.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n\r\n1. **Input Validation**: Ensure that all inputs are validated against a strict set of rules. Use whitelisting to allow only known good data.\r\n2. **Sanitization**: Sanitize inputs to remove any potentially harmful characters or patterns.\r\n3. **Use of Libraries**: Utilize well-maintained libraries and frameworks that provide built-in protection against common vulnerabilities.\r\n4. **Regular Updates**: Keep your Java environment and dependencies up to date with the latest security patches.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\n\r\nTo address this vulnerability, review the code for any input handling logic. Ensure that all inputs are validated and sanitized before processing. Here is a general example of how you might improve input validation in Java:\r\n\r\n```java\r\nimport java.util.regex.Pattern;\r\n\r\npublic class InputValidator {\r\n    private static final Pattern VALID_INPUT_PATTERN = Pattern.compile(\"^[a-zA-Z0-9]+$\");\r\n\r\n    public static boolean isValidInput(String input) {\r\n        return VALID_INPUT_PATTERN.matcher(input).matches();\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\r\n        String userInput = \"exampleInput\";\r\n        if (isValidInput(userInput)) {\r\n            System.out.println(\"Valid input.\");\r\n        } else {\r\n            System.out.println(\"Invalid input.\");\r\n        }\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### OWASP Resources\r\n\r\n- [OWASP Input Validation Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Input_Validation_Cheat_Sheet.html)\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n\r\n- [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)"
