              "id": "glog-ba574f43-0e9e-4c3c-bce5-28cbafd37568",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\n**CVE-2013-1927** is a vulnerability found in the `pkg` component of Java, specifically affecting the Open Source Software (OSS) ecosystem. This vulnerability arises from improper handling of certain input data, which can lead to a denial of service (DoS) or potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code. The issue is primarily due to insufficient validation of user-supplied input, which can be exploited by an attacker to cause the application to crash or execute unintended commands.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Input Validation**: Ensure that all input data is properly validated and sanitized. Implement strict input validation rules to prevent malicious data from being processed by the application.\n\n2. **Update and Patch**: Regularly update your software to the latest version. Apply patches provided by the software maintainers as soon as they are available.\n\n3. **Use Security Libraries**: Utilize security libraries and frameworks that provide built-in protection against common vulnerabilities.\n\n4. **Access Controls**: Implement proper access controls to limit the exposure of vulnerable components to potential attackers.\n\n5. **Monitoring and Logging**: Set up monitoring and logging to detect and respond to suspicious activities promptly.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo address this vulnerability, review the code handling input data in the `pkg` component. Ensure that all inputs are validated against a whitelist of acceptable values. For example, if the input is expected to be a number, use a regular expression to enforce this constraint:\n\n```java\nimport java.util.regex.Pattern;\n\npublic class InputValidator {\n    private static final Pattern NUMBER_PATTERN = Pattern.compile(\"\\\\d+\");\n\n    public static boolean isValidNumber(String input) {\n        return NUMBER_PATTERN.matcher(input).matches();\n    }\n}\n```\n\nIncorporate this validation logic wherever user input is processed to prevent the injection of malicious data.\n\n### OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Cheat Sheet Series](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/)\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)\n\nPlease ensure that the links provided are accessible and valid for anonymous users."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2013-1927/suse:java:"
                ]
              }
            },
