            {
              "id": "glog-3b747d65-0937-4a47-b186-ac97b8942ad1",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe vulnerability identified as **CVE-2021-29563** affects the `tensorflow` package, specifically version `2.1.0`, available on PyPI. This vulnerability arises from a flaw in the implementation of the `tf.raw_ops.SparseFillEmptyRows` operation. The issue is due to a lack of validation on the input arguments, which can lead to a heap buffer overflow. This can potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service (DoS) by crashing the application.\n\n### Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. **Upgrade TensorFlow**: Update to a version of TensorFlow where this vulnerability is patched. The TensorFlow team has addressed this issue in later releases, so upgrading to the latest stable version is advised.\n\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement additional input validation checks in your application to ensure that inputs to TensorFlow operations are within expected bounds and types.\n\n3. **Security Patches**: Regularly apply security patches and updates to your dependencies to protect against known vulnerabilities.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe TensorFlow maintainers have fixed this issue in later versions by adding proper validation checks for the input arguments of the `tf.raw_ops.SparseFillEmptyRows` operation. If you are unable to upgrade, consider backporting the fix from the TensorFlow repository to your version. The fix involves adding checks to ensure that the input tensors are not malformed and that their dimensions are as expected.\n\n### Relevant Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/): A list of the top ten security risks for web applications, which can provide general guidance on secure coding practices.\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/): A quick reference guide for secure coding practices.\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\nThis vulnerability is related to **CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write**. This CWE pertains to writing data past the end, or before the beginning, of the intended buffer, which can lead to unexpected behavior or security vulnerabilities.\n\nFor more information, you can visit the [CWE-787 page](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2021-29563/pkg:pypi/tensorflow@2.1.0"
                ]
              }
