              "id": "glog-41ee5f66-e2e4-478c-acf2-a56c2bab0345",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\n\nThe vulnerability identified as **CVE-2022-25882** affects the `onnx` package, specifically version `1.7.0`, available on PyPI. This vulnerability is related to the improper handling of certain inputs, which can lead to a Denial of Service (DoS) attack. The issue arises from the way the package processes specific data structures, potentially allowing an attacker to craft inputs that consume excessive resources, leading to application slowdown or crash.\n\n### General Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Upgrade the Package**: The most effective mitigation is to upgrade the `onnx` package to a version where this vulnerability is patched. Check the [official ONNX repository](https://github.com/onnx/onnx) for the latest secure version.\n\n2. **Input Validation**: Implement strict input validation to ensure that only well-formed data is processed by the application. This can help prevent malformed inputs from triggering the vulnerability.\n\n3. **Resource Limiting**: Consider implementing resource limits within your application to prevent excessive resource consumption. This can include setting timeouts and memory limits for processing operations.\n\n4. **Monitoring and Logging**: Implement monitoring and logging to detect unusual patterns that may indicate an attempted exploitation of this vulnerability.\n\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nTo address this vulnerability, the maintainers of the `onnx` package would need to ensure that input data is properly validated and sanitized before processing. This might involve:\n\n- Adding checks to ensure that data structures are within expected size and complexity limits.\n- Implementing error handling to gracefully manage unexpected or malformed inputs.\n\nDevelopers using the package should also ensure that they are using the latest version and apply any patches provided by the maintainers.\n\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/): A list of the most critical security risks to web applications.\n- [OWASP Cheat Sheet Series](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/): A collection of high-value information on specific application security topics.\n\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\nThis vulnerability is related to **CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption ('Resource Exhaustion')**. More information can be found on the [CWE website](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/400.html).\n\nPlease ensure to verify the links and their accessibility as they may change over time."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "CVE-2022-25882/pkg:pypi/onnx@1.7.0"
                ]
              }
