              "id": "glog-73463c0d-5c40-45b1-8f77-458998cc9cbc",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "### Description\r\n\r\n**Vulnerability ID:** MAL-2025-3088\r\n\r\n**Affected Component:** `pkg core` in the OSS programming language\r\n\r\n**Vulnerability Type:** This vulnerability is a security flaw in the `pkg core` component of the OSS programming language, which could potentially allow an attacker to execute arbitrary code or cause a denial of service. The issue arises from improper input validation, leading to buffer overflow conditions.\r\n\r\n### General Mitigation Advice\r\n\r\n1. **Input Validation:** Ensure that all inputs are properly validated and sanitized. Implement strict checks on input size and format to prevent buffer overflow conditions.\r\n2. **Update and Patch:** Regularly update the OSS programming language and apply patches provided by the maintainers to address known vulnerabilities.\r\n3. **Use Security Tools:** Employ static analysis tools to detect potential vulnerabilities in the codebase.\r\n4. **Access Controls:** Limit access to the vulnerable component to trusted users only and enforce the principle of least privilege.\r\n\r\n### Source Code Fix Recommendation\r\n\r\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, consider the following code changes:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\n// Example of vulnerable code\r\nvoid processInput(char *input) {\r\n    char buffer[256];\r\n    strcpy(buffer, input); // Vulnerable to buffer overflow\r\n}\r\n\r\n// Recommended fix\r\nvoid processInput(char *input) {\r\n    char buffer[256];\r\n    strncpy(buffer, input, sizeof(buffer) - 1); // Use strncpy to prevent overflow\r\n    buffer[sizeof(buffer) - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Relevant OWASP Resources\r\n\r\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\r\n- [OWASP Secure Coding Practices](https://owasp.org/www-project-secure-coding-practices-quick-reference-guide/)\r\n\r\n### Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\r\n\r\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "MAL-2025-3088/@pump.fun:core:"
                ]
              }
            },
